# L4-8 / C7 (docs/plans/l4-upgrade.md §5-bis) — la contraddizione come STATO: un
# fatto e la sua negazione esplicita, detti in conversazione, sono un urto
# registrato; la lezione che lo crea lo dice, la domanda polare e il «why»
# mostrano le due parti, «What contradicts what?» li elenca, e chi riafferma
# una parte la fa valere (l'altra riceve lo strato settled, non si cancella).

!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset
[test l'urto come stato]
!timeout 4
> What contradicts what?
<~ Nothing that I know of
> Espresso is a coffee.
<~ Learned
> Espresso is not a coffee.
<~ now I hold a contradiction: espresso is a coffee
> Is espresso a coffee?
<~ You told me both that espresso is a coffee
> The kettle leaks current.
> The kettle does not leak current.
<~ contradiction: kettle leaks current
> Does the kettle leak current?
<~ You told me both that kettle leaks current and the opposite
> What do you know about the kettle?
<~ But I hold a contradiction there: you told me both that kettle leaks current and the opposite.
> What contradicts what?
<~ whether espresso is a coffee and whether kettle leaks current
> Espresso is a coffee.
<~ Settled: espresso is a coffee. I no longer hold the opposite
> Is espresso a coffee?
<~ Yes
> What contradicts what?
<~ whether kettle leaks current
<! espresso
> Is water wet?
<! You told me both
> The kettle does not leak current.
<~ Settled: it is not true that kettle leaks current
> Does the kettle leak current?
<~ No
> What contradicts what?
<~ Nothing that I know of

[test l'urto fra classi]
!timeout 4
> Nothing is both a fish and a bird.
<~ Held: nothing is both a fish and a bird.
> Nemo is a fish.
> Is Nemo a fish?
<~ Yes
> Nemo is a bird.
<~ cannot both apply
> Is Nemo a bird?
<~ You told me that nemo is a fish and also that it is a bird
> What contradicts what?
<~ whether nemo is a fish or a bird
> Nemo is a fish.
> Is Nemo a bird?
<! You told me
<! Yes
> Is Nemo a fish?
<~ Yes
> What contradicts what?
<~ Nothing that I know of

[test la lezione «A X cannot be a Y» insegna l'incompatibilita', non una capacita' negata]
!timeout 4
> A cat cannot be a fish.
<~ Held: nothing is both a cat and a fish.
> Tom is a cat.
> Tom is a fish.
<~ cannot both apply
> Is Tom a fish?
<~ tom is a mammal (as a cat) and also that it is a fish, and nothing is both
> A penguin cannot fly.
> Can a penguin fly?
<~ No
!reset
